# GitLab backend sync

When you change **backend** code (`apps/api/**`, `packages/**` used by the API, `workers/**`, or cutover scripts under `scripts/cutover/**`), after committing to GitHub also sync to GitLab when on a branch meant for DevOps (e.g. `cutover/no-supabase` or `master` after cutover merge):

```powershell
powershell -File scripts/sync-backend-to-gitlab.ps1 -Message "<same conventional message>"
```

- Remote: `http://gitlab.lstech-hq.lstechinc.com/websites/backlink-agent.git`
- Branch: `ba-backend`
- Do **not** push web/UI to `ba-backend` (that is `ba-frontend`)
- Skip sync for docs-only / web-only / companion-only changes
